Original commit body from 48b4fe1:

The Make analyzer was emitting a separate symbol for each variable
assignment line (e.g., ASFLAGS := x, ASFLAGS += y, ASFLAGS += z
produced 3 symbols). Now it only emits one symbol per variable name
(the first definition), which is the standard behavior for other
language analyzers.

This fixes the Key Symbols section showing duplicate entries like:
- `ASFLAGS` (variable) ★
- `ASFLAGS` (variable) ★
- `ASFLAGS` (variable) ★
